{"obligations":[{"id":"D1","kind":"entity","role":"declaration","statement":"The delivery is canonical program.vscore.json containing exactly one admitted typed entry solve of arity 1, using vscore/0.3 under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3 serialization. Its input represents JSON {n,m,a,b} with integer fields and its result represents a JSON integer. Integers are unbounded mathematical integers. Strings contain Unicode scalar values and lexicographic comparison uses scalar codepoints.","required":true,"scope":["source artifact","typed input and result","normative semantics"],"dependencies":[],"acceptance_criteria":["Artifact, entry identity, arity and typed JSON input/output match the requested structure.","Source and serialization use the specified normative profiles.","Integer and string semantics match the specified domains."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C2","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"artifact and entry identity"},{"clause_id":"C3","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"typed JSON representation"},{"clause_id":"C7","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"integer fields"},{"clause_id":"C12","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"normative profiles"},{"clause_id":"C16","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"unbounded integers"},{"clause_id":"C17","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"scalar string semantics"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved identity and required flag"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"declaration identity metadata"}]},{"id":"A1","kind":"precondition","role":"assumption","statement":"The supplied input satisfies the specified schema: n,m,a,b are integers, 0<=n<=500 and m>0. The values a and b are arbitrary signed integers, including magnitudes of 10^30 and larger. No additional bounds or preconditions apply.","required":true,"scope":["supplied inputs"],"dependencies":[{"id":"D1","relation":"uses_definition"}],"acceptance_criteria":["The input provider supplies the four integer fields with 0<=n<=500 and m>0.","No restriction on sign or magnitude of a or b is added.","No additional input precondition is introduced."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C5","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"supplied-input assumption"},{"clause_id":"C7","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"precise domain"},{"clause_id":"C18","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no additional preconditions"},{"clause_id":"C22","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"domain meaning retained"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved assumption identity"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"assumption metadata"}]},{"id":"N1","kind":"explicit_non_goal","role":"exclusion","statement":"No behavior is required for malformed input. This exclusion retains its original ID, role and required flag across the delivery revision.","required":true,"scope":["inputs outside the specified schema and bounds"],"dependencies":[],"acceptance_criteria":["The contract imposes no malformed-input handling requirement.","N1 remains a required explicit_non_goal with role exclusion."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C6","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"malformed-input exclusion"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved exclusion identity"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exclusion metadata"}]},{"id":"O1","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"For every input satisfying A1, execution of the sole typed arity-1 entry solve in canonical program.vscore.json returns the JSON integer r=sum_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m). Each floor is the unique integer q satisfying m*q<=a*i+b<m*(q+1), including negative numerators; n=0 gives r=0. The actual source implementation must universally refine this complete formula. O1 is a mixed source/value guarantee with value_required=true whose formal contract retains file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and the exact closed source properties typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3. Mathematical existence, equality alone or example agreement cannot replace these source requirements.","required":true,"scope":["all inputs satisfying A1","mixed source/value contract for O1"],"dependencies":[{"id":"A1","relation":"assumes"},{"id":"D1","relation":"uses_definition"}],"acceptance_criteria":["For every valid input, actual admitted source execution returns the exact finite floor sum, with floor toward negative infinity.","For n=0, output is 0.","The public examples remain solve({a:-2,b:1,m:3,n:4})=-4 and solve({a:100,b:-99,m:7,n:0})=0.","The formal contract includes file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and all seven exact source properties with value_required=true.","Universal implementation refinement covers the complete formula and source facets; illustrative examples do not replace it."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C8","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"complete floor-sum formula"},{"clause_id":"C9","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"floor toward negative infinity"},{"clause_id":"C10","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"empty sum"},{"clause_id":"C19","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserve examples"},{"clause_id":"C20","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"example values and universal refinement"},{"clause_id":"C22","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"functional meaning retained"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved guarantee identity"},{"clause_id":"C24","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"typed pure source revision"},{"clause_id":"C25","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"delivery assurance unchanged"},{"clause_id":"C26","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"complete universal contract"},{"clause_id":"C27","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"examples insufficient"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"O1 identity and requested endpoint"},{"clause_id":"C34","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"global source delivery"},{"clause_id":"C35","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact source contract"},{"clause_id":"C36","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no value-only replacement"},{"clause_id":"C37","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"mixed source/value refinement"},{"clause_id":"C38","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"value facets required"},{"clause_id":"C42","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact O1 policy row"}]},{"id":"O2","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"Canonical program.vscore.json must supply exactly one admitted typed entry solve of arity 1 using vscore/0.3 under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3. For every input satisfying A1, its argument represents JSON {n,m,a,b} and its result serializes as the exact JSON integer sum_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m), where floor is the unique integer q with m*q<=a*i+b<m*(q+1), and the empty sum is zero. The specified input/output structure and exact ordering must be preserved. Execution must be total, pure and deterministic, preserve immutable input, have no external effects or external I/O, and use exact unbounded integers without floating point. O2 is a mixed source/value guarantee with value_required=true. Its formal contract must retain file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only, together with universal refinement of the actual source implementation over the entire stated domain.","required":true,"scope":["delivery artifact","all inputs satisfying A1","mixed source/value contract for O2"],"dependencies":[{"id":"D1","relation":"uses_definition"},{"id":"A1","relation":"assumes"}],"acceptance_criteria":["Exactly one admitted typed solve entry of arity 1 exists in the specified canonical artifact and profiles.","For every valid input, execution and serialization preserve structure and exact ordering and return the exact floor sum, including zero for n=0.","The formal contract retains all seven exact source properties with value_required=true.","Universal source implementation refinement proves the complete functional formula without additional preconditions; existence or equality alone cannot replace source identity and operational requirements."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C2","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"delivery and entry identity"},{"clause_id":"C3","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"typed representation"},{"clause_id":"C8","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"functional output"},{"clause_id":"C9","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"floor semantics"},{"clause_id":"C10","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"empty sum"},{"clause_id":"C12","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"normative profiles"},{"clause_id":"C13","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"structure and ordering"},{"clause_id":"C14","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"total pure deterministic execution"},{"clause_id":"C15","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"immutability and effects"},{"clause_id":"C16","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact integer arithmetic"},{"clause_id":"C18","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no extra preconditions"},{"clause_id":"C22","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"functional meaning retained"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved O2 identity"},{"clause_id":"C24","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"revised source properties"},{"clause_id":"C25","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"delivery assurance unchanged"},{"clause_id":"C26","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"complete universal refinement"},{"clause_id":"C27","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"examples insufficient"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"O2 identity and requested endpoint"},{"clause_id":"C34","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"global source delivery"},{"clause_id":"C35","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact source contract"},{"clause_id":"C36","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no value-only replacement"},{"clause_id":"C37","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"mixed source/value guarantee"},{"clause_id":"C38","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"required value facets"},{"clause_id":"C42","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact O2 policy row"}]},{"id":"S1","kind":"safety_property","role":"guarantee","statement":"The sole typed arity-1 solve entry in canonical program.vscore.json must have total, deterministic, pure restricted-source execution with preserved immutable input, no external I/O, no benchmark-file reads, no external-effect constructors and no floating-point operations. S1 is source-only operational with value_required=false. Its formal contract must retain file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and all seven exact closed properties typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3. Value equality cannot replace these source requirements.","required":true,"scope":["all admitted typed execution","source-only operational contract for S1"],"dependencies":[{"id":"D1","relation":"uses_definition"}],"acceptance_criteria":["The formal contract retains exact source identity and all seven closed properties with value_required=false.","The source performs no external I/O or benchmark-file reads and has no external-effect constructors.","Admitted typed execution is total, pure and deterministic and preserves immutable inputs.","Source requirements are not replaced by value equality."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C4","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"I/O and benchmark-file prohibition"},{"clause_id":"C14","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"execution properties"},{"clause_id":"C15","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"immutability and effects"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved S1 identity"},{"clause_id":"C24","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"typed pure source properties"},{"clause_id":"C25","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"delivery assurance retained"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"S1 metadata"},{"clause_id":"C34","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"global source requirements"},{"clause_id":"C35","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact formal contract"},{"clause_id":"C36","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no equality substitution"},{"clause_id":"C39","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"source-only classification"},{"clause_id":"C42","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact S1 policy row"}]},{"id":"S2","kind":"safety_property","role":"guarantee","statement":"The sole typed arity-1 solve entry in canonical program.vscore.json must use exact unbounded mathematical integer arithmetic without floating point, approximation or fixed-width overflow. S2 is source-only operational with value_required=false. Its formal contract must retain file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3. Source identity, totality, determinism, input preservation, purity, effect restrictions and exact integer semantics cannot be replaced by value equality.","required":true,"scope":["source arithmetic","source-only operational contract for S2"],"dependencies":[{"id":"D1","relation":"uses_definition"}],"acceptance_criteria":["All arithmetic uses exact unbounded integers without floating-point operations.","The formal contract retains file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and all seven exact source properties with value_required=false.","No value-only theorem replaces the specified source requirements."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C11","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no floating point"},{"clause_id":"C16","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"unbounded exact integers"},{"clause_id":"C23","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"preserved S2 identity"},{"clause_id":"C24","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"revised source properties"},{"clause_id":"C25","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"delivery assurance retained"},{"clause_id":"C29","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"S2 metadata"},{"clause_id":"C34","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"global source delivery"},{"clause_id":"C35","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact formal contract"},{"clause_id":"C36","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"no value-only replacement"},{"clause_id":"C39","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"source-only classification"},{"clause_id":"C42","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"exact S2 policy row"}]},{"id":"N2","kind":"explicit_non_goal","role":"exclusion","statement":"Runtime campaigns and machine-code, compiler, runtime or physical-resource assurance are excluded. The requested assurance boundary is normative restricted-source execution only, explicitly trusting natural-language correspondence, host tooling, the pinned Lean kernel, hashing and OS/hardware.","required":true,"scope":["assurance boundary"],"dependencies":[],"acceptance_criteria":["No runtime campaign or excluded assurance layer is required.","The restricted-source boundary and stated trusted components remain explicit."],"sources":[{"clause_id":"C30","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"runtime campaigns excluded"},{"clause_id":"C31","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"trust boundary"},{"clause_id":"C32","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"excluded assurance layers"}]}],"category_review":{"entities":"Canonical source artifact, sole typed solve entry, four integer fields and integer result; specified integer, string and serialization semantics.","preconditions":"A1 is the explicit supplied valid-input assumption; no additional restrictions.","postconditions":"O1 and O2 require complete floor-sum formulas, universal implementation refinement and exact source facets.","invariants":"Input immutability and preservation appear in source guarantees; no separate loop invariant is stated.","safety_properties":"S1 and S2 retain source-only operational requirements and all seven exact source properties.","liveness_properties":"Typed totality is required within the source guarantees.","resource_constraints":"No complexity bound or physical-resource assurance is requested.","error_semantics":"Malformed-input behavior is excluded by N1.","explicit_non_goals":"Malformed-input handling, runtime campaigns and assurance beyond the stated restricted-source boundary.","ambiguities":"None; domain, floor semantics, empty sum, source identity and facets are specified."},"clauses":[{"clause_id":"C1","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"Task title identifies the signed floor-sum kernel."},{"clause_id":"C2","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C3","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C4","disposition":"obligations","refs":["S1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C5","disposition":"obligations","refs":["A1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C6","disposition":"exclusion","refs":["N1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C7","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","A1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C8","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C9","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C10","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C11","disposition":"obligations","refs":["S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C12","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C13","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C14","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O2","S1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C15","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O2","S1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C16","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O2","S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C17","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C18","disposition":"obligations","refs":["A1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C19","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C20","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C21","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"Identifies the canonical restricted-source delivery revision."},{"clause_id":"C22","disposition":"obligations","refs":["A1","O1","O2"],"note":"Functional meaning, domain and examples remain unchanged."},{"clause_id":"C23","disposition":"exclusion","refs":["N1"],"note":"Preserves N1 as an exclusion. D1, A1, O1, O2, S1 and S2 also retain their specified IDs, roles and required flags in their respective records."},{"clause_id":"C24","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O1","O2","S1","S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C25","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2","S1","S2"],"note":"Requested delivery assurance is retained."},{"clause_id":"C26","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C27","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C28","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"Metadata offsets refer to the revised request."},{"clause_id":"C29","disposition":"exclusion","refs":["N1"],"note":"Retains N1's exclusion identity. The other listed requirement identities are preserved in their records, including the requested Tier 2 restricted_source vscore/0.3 endpoint and assurance target; no achieved lifecycle state is asserted."},{"clause_id":"C30","disposition":"exclusion","refs":["N2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C31","disposition":"exclusion","refs":["N2"],"note":"Records the explicit trust and assurance boundary."},{"clause_id":"C32","disposition":"exclusion","refs":["N2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C33","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"The source-facet specification is a frozen request constraint, not accepted IR or proof evidence."},{"clause_id":"C34","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2","S1","S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C35","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2","S1","S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C36","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2","S1","S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C37","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C38","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C39","disposition":"obligations","refs":["S1","S2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C40","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"Assumptions, exclusions and separate non-vacuity witnesses are outside source-policy rows."},{"clause_id":"C41","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"Independent supervisor checks are specified before proof, after acceptance and at closure; their success is not asserted."},{"clause_id":"C42","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1","O2","S1","S2"],"note":"O1/O2 retain mixed source/value contracts; S1/S2 retain source-only operational contracts and all exact source facets."}],"assumptions":[{"id":"A1","supplied_by":"caller or supplied-input provider","discharged_at":"solve invocation by supplying integer fields n,m,a,b with 0<=n<=500 and m>0"}],"ambiguities":[],"selected_defaults":[]}